// §6.3.4 parameter dependence, for a default whose expression is NOT plain
// arithmetic: "an update of gate_width ... automatically updates gate_cap."
// The clause says nothing about which operators the dependent expression is
// allowed to use, so `exp(a)` tracks `a` exactly as `2.0*a` does.
//
// VerA emits a `derive(model: *Model)` seam that recomputes dependent
// parameters from the CURRENT model values. The renderer behind it (`f64Const`
// in src/backend/codegen.zig) once knew only arithmetic, abs, sqrt, min, max
// and pow; a default it could not render got NO derive line at all and silently
// kept the initializer folded against the DECLARED default of `a`, so `curved`
// froze at exp(2.0) and an override of `a` never reached it. This file was
// `//! xfail` on exactly that. `f64Const` now renders the whole of Table 4-14
// and Table 4-15, so it derives.
//
// The failure mode was silent in exactly the way that matters: the two
// parameters sit side by side, one tracked and one did not, and nothing in the
// source or the diagnostics said which was which. That is why this fixture
// asserts BOTH — a fix that only made `curved` derive while breaking `scaled`
// would still fail, and that is what the arithmetic half is here to catch.
//
// The wants are the two products written out. `a` is overridden to 3.0 below:
//   scaled = 2.0 * 3.0 = 6.0                 (exact in binary)
//   curved = exp(3.0)  = 20.085536923187668  (the double nearest e^3)
//
//! lrm 6.3.4
//! param a = 3.0
`include "check.vh"
module ch6_dependent_transcendental(p);
  inout p;
  electrical p;
  parameter real a = 2.0 from (0:inf);
  // Arithmetic: the control — this half always derived.
  parameter real scaled = 2.0 * a;
  // Transcendental: same §6.3.4 rule, same derive line.
  parameter real curved = exp(a);
  analog begin
    `CHECKX("an arithmetic dependent parameter tracks the override", scaled, 6.0);
    `CHECKR("a transcendental dependent parameter tracks it too", curved,
            20.085536923187668, 1e-15);
    I(p) <+ 0.0;
  end
endmodule
